condition_name: Neonatal Sepsis
condition_slug: neonatal-sepsis
source: NSTG 2022
introduction: A clinical syndrome resulting from bacterial blood stream infection with active proliferation of the organisms. Early-Onset sepsis manifests within the first 72 hours of life or at most 7 days of life while Late-Onset sepsis manifests after 7 days of life.
clinical_features[2]:
  - type: Non-specific features
    features[4]: fever,vomiting,poor feeding,poor activity
  - type: More specific features
    features[3]: hypothermia,convulsions,jaundice
investigations[2]: A lumbar tap for cerebrospinal fluid analysis is mandatory unless the infant has cardio-respiratory instability. It must not delay empirical antibiotic therapy.,"Neuro-imaging studies if fever persists, seizures recur, or occipitofrontal circumference is increasing."
treatment:
  goals[0]:
  non_drug[0]:
  drug[4]: The empirical antibiotic therapy tailored to local patterns.,Ceftriaxone 50 mg/kg 12-hourly or Cefotaxime 50 mg/kg 6-hourly and Gentamicin 2.5 mg/kg 12-hourly.,Intravenous Ampicillin 50 mg/kg 6-hourly in specific cases.,"Phenobarbitone for seizures; 15 mg/kg loading dose, 2.5 mg/kg 12-hourly maintenance."
  adverse_reactions_and_cautions[0]:
  supportive_measures[3]: Fluid therapy with caution against over-hydration.,"Fluid and caloric balance, blood transfusion for severe anaemia.",Oxygen therapy and ventilator support for hypoxaemia.
differential_diagnoses[0]:
complications[0]:
prevention[0]:
other_investigations: null
definitive_treatment: null
prognosis: null